Z||000005||West Coast Fiero||12-30-2001||04:57 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by btoth:<BR><B>When I installed my new IAC last year before I got my new engine I know it wasn't setup to 1-1/8"... is that important?  It ran really bad for a while until I drove it and then I figured it just set itself properly.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>it will set itself up, but in relation to how it came out of the box. The way to depress or extend the plunger is by either pulling or pushing while rocking the plunger shaft side to side, however I have noticed that non-AC DElco brands have different internals which require no side to side movement, but just pushing or pulling.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://clubs.hemmings.com/fieroswest/WestCoast300.gif"> <BR>Eric Nelson<BR>Technician,<BR>West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
